WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.420
Dark Souls 3 has been out a while

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.040
And you might that you know everything about it, but

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.420
Don't underestimate the depth of what this community can discover

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.860
That sound you heard at the start

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.240
That was a voice clip from the Dancer's opening cutscene

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.680
But reversed

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.340
And only less than a week ago, reddit user Sentuh

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:36.420
Noticed that reversing the Dancer's soundclips revealed their haunting original sound

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.940
Honestly, I'm surprised they didn't use these sounds instead

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:52.600
Next, there are two versions of the Handmaiden in the two variations of Firelink Shrine

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.580
One in our enlightened Shrine, and another in the dark Shrine

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.720
Which is connected to the rest of the overworld.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.660
And the question is:

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.620
Are they the same person? And if they are

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:09.240
Is one in the past, and another in the present?

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.460
Well if you talk to the Untended Graves' Handmaiden

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.880
Before you talk to our one,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.400
Then our Handmaiden recognizes us, and

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.840
Gives a tiny bit of unique dialogue at the start:

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.020
So this makes it clear that they're the same person, right

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:43.880
And it also lends credit to the theory that the darkened Shrine appears in the past.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.100
Because she recognizes us.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.920
The shrines are intriguing, and there is a lot more to say

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.600
So I'll try to make a video on this area soon.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.780
The earliest mention I found of this is on integ3r's Youtube channel

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.620
So credit to him for recording it for sure.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.220
One thing sold by the Handmaiden is the Budding Green Blossom

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.180
Which becomes available for ten souls

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.660
When you get to the part of Sirris' quest line

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.760
Where she goes to kill Hodrick

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.660
The interesting thing isn't that it's ten souls

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.680
It's that it has an extra sentence in its description that

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.440
All the others don't have.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.500
It reads:

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.620
"Good-bye, dear Grandmother."

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.000
"I will visit Grandfather, in the Pit of Hollows."

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.660
And if you look closely, you'll see that these flowers

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.820
Are tied with some string, like a bouquet

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.420
This might become a knowledge at this point

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.860
But I came across this discovery when JakMon777

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.280
Twitted the hidden sentence at me and

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:55.320
I couldn't find it in any description I looked at.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.340
Until I looked on the Fextralife Wiki and it had all the information there

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.840
So does this make the Handmaiden the grandmother in the description?

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.440
Or was this bouquet something that the Handmaiden

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.660
Stripped from a grave outside the Shrine?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.700
She does have a habit of accumulating armour sets from corpses after all

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:21.260
For number 4, I loved the discussion that came from the thread made by EtherMoth and Doffymom

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:26.380
Who put forward that each of the unkindled NPCs in Dark Souls 3

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.380
Have a link to a Lord of Cinder.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.860
Anri to Aldrich

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.800
Siegward to Yhorm and

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.800
Hawkwood to his Legion.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:37.720
We've talked before about how it's an Unkindled's duty

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.440
To place the cinders of Lords upon their thrones, and

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.360
Each unkindled is somehow invested in the death

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.280
Of their corresponding Lords.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.000
The fourth Lord, of course, are the twin Princes, and

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.020
It's not too far-fetched to think that we

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.120
Are their corresponding Unkindled.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.280
along with the others as

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.880
Those with the highest chance to uphold their duty

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.520
And bring the Lords we're associated with to their thrones

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.880
You should really check out the discussion going on in the link in the description, because

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.260
There is a lot more to be said on this topic

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.920
I think it's an awesome discovery

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.120
Also, in Firelink Shrine

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.780
Have you ever had the Firekeeper turn away from you?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.720
This happens if you wear the Untrue Dark Ring

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.300
Or the Untrue White Ring

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.320
Which are rings that reference the deeply detested Hollows of Londor

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.620
So, is she turning away from you in disgust?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:40.300
This was first posted about by SaviorG and then again by sciritai6 with more proof

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.600
I tested it too and I could never get the Firekeeper to turn away

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.740
Without the ring on and without being hollowed

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.500
So it's undeniable I think that

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.840
This turn has something to do with the rings and

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.780
Perhaps with the Hollows of Londor as well right?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:00.920
So let me know if she exhibits this exact same behaviour for you guys as well

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.600
It would be good to get some more tests out there I think

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.580
Because some people have been reporting that

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.400
She turns away without the rings on for them

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.220
But I could never get her to do it without the rings

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.740
6 is probably the biggest long shot on the list but

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.680
I still think it has merit to it

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.700
Three months ago, KronosTrinity pointed out that

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.520
The Shrine's Handmaiden has unique dialogue

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.300
For the Dreamchaser's ashes

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.940
Which are the ashes that you find atop Farron Keep

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.980
Behind the illusory wall

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.800
And he or she also points out that

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:36.420
The hand in these ashes clutches a pendant

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:03.900
In Dark Souls 1, finding meaning for this pendant starting item became

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.580
This long running challenge and then joke

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:07.780
Of the series because

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.560
The series' creator Miyazaki mentioned that

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.000
He'd like to select the pendant himself, personally

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:18.460
And later he admitted that the pendant was a bit of a prank

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.800
Intended to keep the players guessing at its purpose

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.780
For, in this game full of secrets

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.480
How could such a thing be meaningless right?

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.560
So is the Handmaiden poking fun at

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.540
Whoever's clutching the pendant?

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.760
Are the creators making fun of us

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.540
For clinging to these lofty dreams?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:43.340
Number 7 is a relatively recent discovery for how amazing it is

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.580
So around three weeks ago, user Skarekrow13 over on the Fextralife forum

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.920
Posted this exhaustive breakdown of how he

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.420
Deciphered the runes upon the titanite slabs in Dark Souls 3

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:00.260
And his interpretation is that every symbol line

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:03.740
Describes a different historical age in the series

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.300
He roughly translates line 1 to:

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.220
Skarekrow stresses that there is a great deal of

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:50.960
Personal bias involved in anyone's interpretation

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.360
Of these runes and these symbols

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.580
Including his own bias, so

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:59.020
I really really encourage you to read his article on the topic, because

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.200
Your interpretation serves a really big part in this as well

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.300
It's crazy that this could go undiscovered for so long

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:11.260
Moving on, did you ever do a visceral attack on one of the Pontiff's beasts, but

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.760
Not finish it off when it was vulnerable?

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:18.000
The first post I can find on this is by GNLink34

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.880
Whose post got a ton of attention about three months ago

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:27.100
To me, more than anything, this helps cement Pontiff's Sulyvahn's character

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:31.320
Because he was the one responsible for these beings becoming this way

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.960
He was a tyrant, a man with twisted morals who

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:38.460
Transformed his own men into these beasts

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:42.520
And yet it's clear that some of these beasts' humanity

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.780
It still remains, and they are either begging for mercy here

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.400
Or they're praying in desperation

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:54.740
The next thing is that Anri has unique piece of dialogue and interaction

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:58.900
If you execute Horace while they're along the Path of Sacrifices

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:32.780
And finally, something I wish I knew in my last video

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.980
The comment section caught me up on this

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:38.280
So there is this statue in Lower Lothric

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:44.440
And user Hoototo points out the links between it and Pontiff Sulyvahn

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:48.000
First, this statue holds the Profaned Great Sword

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.900
Which is a weapon wielded by Sulyvahn, and

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.420
This weapon also references him

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:55.660
When he was still a young sorcerer

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.860
Second, the bracelet that the statue has is

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.820
The same as the bracelet on Sulyvahn's right arm

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.760
And you might think, you know, okay

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:09.560
A few reused assets, big deal, From does this all the time

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:13.860
But this statue linking Lothric and young Sulyvahn

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.080
It's a huge deal

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.220
If you watched the Angels video

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.620
Then you'll know that I talked a lot about how

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:23.400
The Lothric bloodline and the sorcerers of the Grand Archives

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.840
Rose together. They were very close

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.020
And I also said that

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:31.540
The first of the Scholars played a part in convincing

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:35.180
The young Lord Lothric against the linking of the flame

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:38.280
And the Pontiff is this character that

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:41.560
Really does go against the linking of the flame as well

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.780
So he's a huge candidate for being the First of the Scholars

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:51.180
This character who convinced Lothric not to link the fire

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:54.600
And additionally, the Pontiff's gear looks

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:58.480
A lot like the candlestick Scholars of the Grand Archives

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.020
So it seems pretty clear to me

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:06.020
That Sulyvahn might be responsible for convincing Lothric not to link the fire.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:09.380
And that he might be very much responsible

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.720
For the defection of the Deacons of the Deep away

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:13.900
From the Way of White

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.800
For the fall of Lothric's bloodline and

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.400
Basically for most of the events in the game

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:24.060
Before you go, I've got one thing to ask of you guy

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:26.760
And it's not to like this video, it's instead

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:29.420
To go and send some love and some friendly mail

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.880
To the people I featured in this video

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:34.160
To read their contributions and

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:38.420
To continue supporting the incredible discoveries of everybody in this community

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:41.040
Because I'm just happy I can be a platform

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.180
To display and discuss some of this stuff

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.240
Also, why the fuck is there a crab in the ball??

